  "question": {
    "text": "The number of ways in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></math> distinct letters (addressed) can be distributed in <math><mi>N</mi></math> distinct mail boxes such that there are exactly <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> letters <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> in one of the mail boxes is"
